{"name":"Badlands","hex":"#b5695a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Badlands","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Badlands National Park, a national park in South Dakota."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Badlands"}],"entries":[{"title":"Badlands","blocks":[{"text":"Badlands are a type of dry terrain where softer sedimentary rocks and clay-rich soils have been extensively eroded. They are characterized by steep slopes, minimal vegetation, lack of a substantial regolith, and high drainage density. Ravines, gullies, buttes, hoodoos and other such geologic forms are common in badlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Chinle_Badlands.jpg/330px-Chinle_Badlands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badlands","wikidata":"Q272921"},{"title":"Badlands (Halsey album)","blocks":[{"text":"Badlands is the debut studio album by American singer Halsey. It was released on August 28, 2015 through Astralwerks. Musically, Badlands is an electropop, alternative pop, dark pop, and synth-pop record featuring industrial undertones. Halsey wrote every song on the album when she was 19, while production was handled by a number of producers. Norwegian producer Lido was one of the main producers on Badlands."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4c/Halsey_-_Badlands.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badlands_(Halsey_album)","wikidata":"Q20058569"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg/330px-A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theod